{
  "_comment": "SHARED UI-element library for flicker clients: a flat map of named UI-element definitions, loaded into a ScriptHost and exposed to Lua as the `UI` global; each client's scripts read the elements they need by name (unused keys are ignored). Front-end shell (inherited by every client): `modal` (shared component style) + `screens.*` (its instances, selected by Model.screen) + `settings` + `logo` + `loading`. Per-client in-game HUDs are added here too, keyed by element name: `hud` = flicker-csg. Colors are RGBA 0..1; positions/sizes are HUD pixels; `texture` names resolve through the `Textures` global. As more clients migrate, add their HUD element(s) here — namespace the key if it would collide (e.g. two clients both wanting `hud`).",

